pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% POSITIVE CONTROL for the `conclusion BOUNDS` fix. Refusing a bound while a SOLUTION-EXCLUDING
% constraint is live must not touch the ordinary branch-and-bound argument, where the database
% contradiction comes from an OBJECTIVE-IMPROVING constraint: `soli` logs the value-1 solution,
% installs "objective <= 0", and that is contradictory with the formula. This is the shape the
% whole optimisation track rests on and it must keep verifying.
f 1;
soli x1 ~x2 : 1;
rup >= 1;
output NONE;
conclusion BOUNDS 1 1;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
